  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Texas received $410M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations are down 99.6% year over year, with 851 awards and an average award size of $482K. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in Texas, awarding $371M so far this fiscal year. AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC is the largest vendor by dollars with $164M, followed by LUMEN TECHNOLOGIES GOVERNMENT SOLUTIONS, INC. with $77.6M. Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the largest industry by obligations at $242M. Historical context shows large swings: FY22 obligations were $67.6B, FY23 obligations were $81.9B, FY24 obligations were $59.3B, FY25 obligations were $86.4B, and FY26 obligations were $100B, before FY27 obligations of $410M. Transactions in FY2027 to date concentrate heavily in telecommunications and veterans services spending. Contract activity levels and average award size indicate that the current fiscal year is a partial picture. Vendors in logistics, health services, and technology appear among the top recipients, reflecting a mix of communications, medical, and IT-related obligations in Texas.",
